WEBVTT

00:00:07.957 --> 00:00:09.957
Again, you're gone

00:00:11.597 --> 00:00:14.717
Off on a diff'rent path
than mine

00:00:14.877 --> 00:00:16.637
I'm left behind

00:00:16.797 --> 00:00:21.157
Wondering if I should follow

00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:23.877
You had to go

00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:28.837
And, of course,
it's always fine

00:00:29.477 --> 00:00:34.757
I prob'ly could catch up
with you tomorrow

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:41.997
But is this what it feels like
to be growing apart?

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:45.117
When did I become the one

00:00:45.197 --> 00:00:48.837
Who's always
chasing your heart?

00:00:49.197 --> 00:00:51.637
BOTH: Now I turn around
and find

00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:54.997
I am lost in the woods

00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:58.437
North is South
Right is left

00:00:58.597 --> 00:01:01.717
When you're gone

00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:04.517
I'm the one who sees you home

00:01:04.677 --> 00:01:08.317
But now I'm lost in the woods

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:13.317
And I don't know
what path you are on

00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:16.837
I'm lost in the woods

00:01:21.037 --> 00:01:23.197
Up till now

00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:27.157
The next step
was a question of how

00:01:27.557 --> 00:01:32.957
I never thought it was
a question of whether

00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:35.517
Who am I

00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:40.237
If I'm not your guy?

00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:45.437
Where am I
if we're not together?

00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:48.997
Forever

00:01:49.157 --> 00:01:51.877
Now I know
you're my true North

00:01:51.957 --> 00:01:55.397
'Cause I am lost in the woods

00:01:55.557 --> 00:01:58.237
Up is down
Day is night

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.797
When you're not there

00:02:01.957 --> 00:02:04.677
Oh, you're my only landmark

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:08.437
So I'm lost in the woods

00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:13.317
Wondering if you still care

00:02:14.237 --> 00:02:16.877
But I'll wait

00:02:17.877 --> 00:02:19.957
For a sign

00:02:20.037 --> 00:02:23.757
-For a sign
-That I'm your path

00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.517
-'Cause you are mine
-You are mine

00:02:27.597 --> 00:02:29.477
Until then

00:02:29.637 --> 00:02:33.517
-I'm lost in the woods
-Lost in the woods

00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:36.077
In the woods
Lost in the woods

00:02:36.157 --> 00:02:37.717
I'm lost in the woods

00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:41.917
Lost in the woods
I'm lost

00:02:42.437 --> 00:02:47.637
I'm lost in the woods

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:52.957
(SVEN GROANS)

00:02:54.877 --> 00:02:55.957
(CROAKS)

00:02:56.957 --> 00:02:58.957
(VOCALIZING)

00:03:02.397 --> 00:03:04.477
-(VOCALIZING OFF-KEY)
-(ANNA GASPS)

00:03:04.957 --> 00:03:05.957
(EXHALES)

00:03:06.397 --> 00:03:08.277
(VOCALIZING)

00:03:08.357 --> 00:03:10.277
-(IMITATES IN OFF-KEY)
-(CREATURE CROAKS)

00:03:11.477 --> 00:03:14.757
Hey, Olaf, um, maybe just
one of you should do it?

00:03:14.957 --> 00:03:16.957
I agree.
She's a little pitchy.

00:03:17.037 --> 00:03:18.077
-(CHITTERING)
-(GRUNTS)

00:03:18.157 --> 00:03:19.957
(GASPS) Hey, Gale's back.

00:03:20.037 --> 00:03:21.717
(CHITTERING)

00:03:21.797 --> 00:03:22.797
(GASPS)

00:03:25.757 --> 00:03:26.797
What?

00:03:33.957 --> 00:03:35.557
(BOTH GASPING)

00:03:35.637 --> 00:03:37.477
How can it be?

00:03:37.637 --> 00:03:38.677
What is it?

00:03:39.877 --> 00:03:41.757
ANNA:
Mother and Father's ship.

00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:44.477
But this isn't
the Southern Sea.

00:03:44.637 --> 00:03:46.837
No, it isn't.

00:03:59.797 --> 00:04:01.477
ELSA: Why is their ship here?

00:04:02.597 --> 00:04:04.237
How is it here?

00:04:05.557 --> 00:04:08.197
It must have been washed in
from the Dark Sea.

00:04:08.357 --> 00:04:10.597
What were they doing
in the Dark Sea?

00:04:12.397 --> 00:04:13.877
I don't know.

00:04:14.437 --> 00:04:16.877
How did the ship
get through the mist?

00:04:17.037 --> 00:04:18.877
I thought nobody could but us.

00:04:19.637 --> 00:04:22.397
Unless nobody was on it.

00:04:23.637 --> 00:04:25.557
There's gotta be
something here.

00:04:25.717 --> 00:04:27.717
Wait. Wait.
Look around.

00:04:28.397 --> 00:04:30.957
Every Arendellian ship
has a compartment.

00:04:31.077 --> 00:04:32.277
Waterproof.

00:04:32.837 --> 00:04:34.757
That's very clever.

00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:36.317
Although,
it does make me wonder

00:04:36.397 --> 00:04:38.317
why they don't just make
the whole ship waterproof.

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:46.037
(GASPS) Here.

00:04:51.997 --> 00:04:54.077
What language is this?

00:04:54.237 --> 00:04:55.637
I don't know.

00:04:55.717 --> 00:04:58.077
But look,
this is Mother's handwriting.

00:04:58.237 --> 00:04:59.717
"The end of the ice age.

00:04:59.877 --> 00:05:01.877
"The river found, but lost.

00:05:02.037 --> 00:05:05.677
"Magic's source.
Elsa's source?"

00:05:08.277 --> 00:05:09.797
(GASPS) It's a map.

00:05:11.797 --> 00:05:13.477
They traveled north

00:05:13.557 --> 00:05:17.277
and planned to cross
the Dark Sea to...

00:05:17.437 --> 00:05:19.277
ELSA: Ahtohallan.

00:05:19.437 --> 00:05:20.917
It's real?

00:05:21.077 --> 00:05:22.197
Octa-who-what?

00:05:22.357 --> 00:05:23.597
Ahtohallan.

00:05:23.797 --> 00:05:25.597
It's a magical river

00:05:25.717 --> 00:05:28.157
said to hold all the answers
about the past.

00:05:28.317 --> 00:05:31.557
Reinforcing my
"water has memory" theory. Mm.

00:05:32.037 --> 00:05:33.677
Water has memory.

00:05:40.357 --> 00:05:41.837
Elsa?

00:05:42.477 --> 00:05:44.917
I wanna know
what happened to them.

